      "hints": [
        "Apply the binomial theorem to expand $(1 + ax)^6$ up to the term in $x^2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Expand $(1 + ax)^6$ in ascending powers of $x$ using the binomial theorem:\n$$(1 + ax)^6 = 1 + \\binom{6}{1}(ax) + \\binom{6}{2}(ax)^2 + \\dots = 1 + 6ax + 15a^2x^2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
