      "hints": [
        "Extract the $x^2$ terms in $(1 - 3x)(1 + 6ax + 15a^2x^2 + \\dots)$: $1(15a^2) + (-3)(6a) = 15a^2 - 18a$.",
        "Equate to $-3$ to get $5a^2 - 6a + 1 = 0$ and factorise."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Identify all products that produce an $x^2$ power in $(1 - 3x)(1 + 6ax + 15a^2x^2 + \\dots)$:\n$$\\text{Terms in } x^2 = [1 \\times 15a^2x^2] + [(-3x) \\times (6ax)] = (15a^2 - 18a)x^2$$",
        "Equate the combined coefficient to $-3$:\n$$15a^2 - 18a = -3 \\implies 15a^2 - 18a + 3 = 0$$",
        "Divide by $3$ and factorise the quadratic equation in $a$:\n$$5a^2 - 6a + 1 = 0 \\implies (5a - 1)(a - 1) = 0$$\n$$a = 1 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = \\frac{1}{5} = 0.2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
